== Std.Terminal: the screen and the keyboard of a text program, such as an
== editor (change console-abi-terminal, canon r3.88, decision F1 of Marcelo
== Fortes, 2026-10-21). The types are declared here; the routines are
== compiler intrinsics carried out by libinoxrt, visible in a program that
== uses Std.Terminal, so their names stay free elsewhere.
==
==   RawMode(On Bool)              == keys one at a time, not echoed; False goes back
==   ReadKey TKey                  == waits for the next key
==   ScreenSize TScreenSize        == rows and columns of the window (24 x 80 if none)
==   MoveTo(Row Integer, Col Integer)  == the cursor, counted from 1
==   ClearScreen                   == clears the window, cursor at 1, 1
==   ClearLine                     == clears the cursor's line
==   SetColor(Fg TColor, Bg TColor)    == the colors of what is written next
==   ResetColor                    == the terminal's own colors
==   ShowCursor(On Bool)           == shows or hides the cursor
==   Flush                         == writes out what is waiting to be shown
==
== Rules:
==   - the terminal is given back as the program found it however the program
==     ends: the end of Main, a runtime error, an exception nobody handles or
==     a signal (raw mode off, cursor shown, colors reset);
==   - when standard input is not a terminal (a file, a pipe) RawMode does
==     nothing and ReadKey reads the same keys from the bytes, so a program
==     can be tested with an input file;
==   - ReadKey past the end of input stops the program with "end of input";
==   - MoveTo with Row or Col below 1 stops the program with "value out of
==     range";
==   - in a key of kind KeyChar, Ch is the character typed; in any other kind
==     Ch is '\0'. Ctrl+A .. Ctrl+Z are KeyChar 'a' .. 'z' with Ctrl;
==     Ctrl+Space is ' ' with Ctrl; Escape then a key is that key with Alt.

Type
    TKeyKind (KeyChar, KeyUp, KeyDown, KeyLeft, KeyRight, KeyHome, KeyEnd, KeyPageUp, KeyPageDown,
              KeyEnter, KeyBackspace, KeyDelete, KeyTab, KeyEscape,
              KeyF1, KeyF2, KeyF3, KeyF4, KeyF5, KeyF6, KeyF7, KeyF8, KeyF9, KeyF10, KeyF11, KeyF12)

    TKey Struct
        Kind TKeyKind := KeyChar
        Ch Char := '\0'
        Ctrl Bool := False
        Alt Bool := False
    ;

    TScreenSize Struct
        Rows Integer := 24
        Cols Integer := 80
    ;

    TColor (Black, Red, Green, Yellow, Blue, Magenta, Cyan, White,
            Gray, BrightRed, BrightGreen, BrightYellow, BrightBlue, BrightMagenta, BrightCyan, BrightWhite)
